     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":4,\"rationale\":\"Four blocks are sufficient: codeRepo:collection, mailArchive:collection, shareMount:collection and dbReplica:collection. These are the four parents of the OR target, so blocking them leaves no way in. Three blocks are not enough. (1) The codeRepo branch needs a block on browserStore, fileServer or codeRepo itself, because browserStore is fed directly by entry footholds. (2) The remaining two blocks would then have to stop mailArchive, shareMount and dbReplica. Stopping mailArchive with one block requires printServer or mailArchive. That leaves one block for both shareMount and dbReplica, and dbReplica needs both monitoringHost (via vpnSession) and hypervisor (via backupHost AND rdpLogin) cut. No single step does both. (3) Stopping mailArchive with two blocks (tokenCache plus vpnSession or sshKey) leaves hypervisor reachable, so dbReplica stays open. Therefore the minimum is 4.\"}"
    }
   ],
